Welcome back to this session on value creation.

3
00:00:08.666 --> 00:00:11.916
Recall that we've been through the specific steps.

4
00:00:11.916 --> 00:00:15.166
Having just looked at improve action settings.

5
00:00:15.166 --> 00:00:21.499
Now, one of the key elements that must occur is to control input variation.

6
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:25.966
Relative to those settings.

7
00:00:25.966 --> 00:00:32.199
See now, those settings in turn, determine what the force will be

8
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:38.200
for each opportunity condition.

9
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:45.133
Which in turn makes change. Which leads to satisfying needs.

10
00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:50.499
So, let's look at that now, as we reduce variation

11
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:56.500
around an action setting, a better action setting, a superior action setting.

12
00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:00.500
The force improves for the condition

13
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:04.766
associated with the opportunity for change.

14
00:01:04.766 --> 00:01:10.999
That in turn, if we can make that change, satisfies the needs.

15
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:16.033
That's really what we're looking at here. So now, let’s look on to controlling input variations.

16
00:01:16.033 --> 00:01:23.099
Recall that we had talked about the example of a newspaper, getting a job.

17
00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:28.133
And that to get an opportunity means we gotta be able to get the newspaper.

18
00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:30.999
But we said, what if there's a dog out there that chews it up

19
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.633
because the newspaper comes at 8 o’clock in the morning. Well, change the time.

20
00:01:34.633 --> 00:01:37.699
So, what we did is we improved that action setting.

21
00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:41.700
We moved it from 8 o'clock in the morning to 6 o'clock in the morning.

22
00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:48.833
Now, what I'm going to do is to put a little bit more understanding around that.

23
00:01:48.833 --> 00:01:55.733
I’m going to come over here and I'm gonna put this scale out, called 8 o'clock a.m.

24
00:01:55.733 --> 00:02:02.733
And remember, we want to change here now to 6 o'clock a.m.

25
00:02:02.733 --> 00:02:07.566
We want to move the time the newspaper is delivered

26
00:02:07.566 --> 00:02:13.166
from eight to six. And recall, that's a gap.

27
00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:15.999
We gotta close that gap.

28
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:22.466
And Y is a function of X. And remember, this is a gap on the X side. I’m just refreshing us.

29
00:02:22.466 --> 00:02:27.599
Now, around that 6 o'clock, there’s variation.

30
00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:32.466
In other words, some mornings, the paper may come at this time.

31
00:02:32.466 --> 00:02:36.466
Other mornings, it may come at this time. So there's a window of variation.

32
00:02:36.466 --> 00:02:40.466
There’s variation around that time.

33
00:02:40.466 --> 00:02:44.799
So, the more that we move in this direction, the greater the probability is

34
00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:49.500
the next door neighbor’s dog is going to chew it up. And that could very well be. Murphy's Law.

35
00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:53.400
The day the newspaper ad comes out for the job we needed.

36
00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.433
See. So we gotta remove that variation.

37
00:02:56.433 --> 00:03:00.433
We don't want variation around these action settings.

38
00:03:00.433 --> 00:03:03.633
Recall, that's an action setting.

39
00:03:03.633 --> 00:03:07.066
That's an action setting. We changed the action setting.

40
00:03:07.066 --> 00:03:13.699
And this is the new one. This is the improved action setting.

41
00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:20.666
And we don't want variation around it. So, what do we do?

42
00:03:20.666 --> 00:03:27.666
Well, let’s think about that a second. Those three words. Those key three words.

43
00:03:27.666 --> 00:03:33.499
Improve. Action.

44
00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:36.600
Settings.

45
00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:42.100
And I add to that, for each critical condition. Whoops, remember that?

46
00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:46.100
In Six Sigma work, we had critical to value, critical to quality.

47
00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:50.100
Now, we have a critical condition.

48
00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:54.100
For which there is an optimal setting for that critical condition.

49
00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:58.100
That setting is an action setting, and we have to improve it.

50
00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:03.300
We’ve gotta take it from where it was, to where we need it to be.

51
00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:07.300
And then minimize the variation around it.

52
00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:13.266
That's absolutely essential. That's what we mean by improve action settings.

53
00:04:13.266 --> 00:04:17.266
Now remember, if we do that,

54
00:04:17.266 --> 00:04:24.066
and control input variations. Control our input variations.

55
00:04:24.066 --> 00:04:29.566
Now remember, if we do that. If we reduce input variations,

56
00:04:29.566 --> 00:04:35.966
then we more assuredly keep the optimal settings.

57
00:04:35.966 --> 00:04:42.899
Associated with each of the forces.

58
00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:47.866
That constitutes the conditions

59
00:04:47.866 --> 00:04:51.866
or opportunities as we call them.

60
00:04:51.866 --> 00:04:55.866
To satisfy our needs.

61
00:04:55.866 --> 00:04:58.832
See that's so simple the way it works.

62
00:04:58.833 --> 00:05:04.033
As a matter of fact, it's so simple it's almost embarrassingly simple.

63
00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:07.599
But you know something? Some of the greatest things are

64
00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:10.833
when the not so obvious becomes obvious.

65
00:05:10.833 --> 00:05:15.766
I love it when people used to tell me about the old breakthrough strategy I invented.

66
00:05:15.766 --> 00:05:21.066
Define, measure, analyze, improve, control. They said, well, we understand that.

67
00:05:21.066 --> 00:05:25.066
My question was, well then, why haven't you been doing for the last 30 years?

68
00:05:25.066 --> 00:05:28.699
Well, that's a part of when something is really good.

69
00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:33.233
When you're able to find simple things and make them obvious.

70
00:05:33.233 --> 00:05:37.299
Bring them from the subconscious to the conscious level.

71
00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:40.266
See, that's all this strategy is really doing.

72
00:05:40.266 --> 00:05:43.266
Many of us already do this in a subconscious way,

73
00:05:43.266 --> 00:05:46.899
but to make it teachable and understandable, to make it habit.

74
00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:52.100
Listen to that. To make it habit, we gotta consciously do it time and time again.

75
00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:56.100
We gotta remove variations around the optimal settings,

76
00:05:56.100 --> 00:06:00.466
for those forces that constitutes the vital few conditions,

77
00:06:00.466 --> 00:06:06.666
of the key opportunities, associated with the value needs that we have in our life.

78
00:06:06.666 --> 00:06:11.666
Thank you for choosing SSMI.
